[
    {
        "content": "<p>Mathlib has a test that makes sure that we have efficient exponentiation in <code>Mod</code>. Unfortunately, it seems that the default exponentiation on <code>Fin</code> is not efficient:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- A 1024-bit prime number</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"n\">xb10b8f96a080e01dde92de5eae5d54ec52c99fbcfb06a3c69a6a9dca52d23b616073e28675a23d189838ef1e2ee652c013ecb4aea906112324975c3cd49b83bfaccbdd7d90c4bd7098488e9c219a73724effd6fae5644738faa31a4ff55bccc0a151af5f0dc8b4bd45bf37df365c1a65e68cfda76d4da708df1fb2bc2e4a4371</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"n\">xa4d1cbd5c3fd34126765a442efb99905f8104dd258ac507fd6406cff14266d31266fea1e5c41564b777e690f5504f213160217b4b01b886a5e91547f9e2749f4d7fbd7d3b9a92ee1909d0d2263f80a76a6a24c087a091f531dbf0a0169b6a28ad662a4d18e73afa32d779d5918d08bc8858f4dcef97c2a24855e6eeb22b3b2e5</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Removing this line breaks the `#eval`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Grind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instPowFinNatOfNeZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Grind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instHPowFinNatOfNeZero</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585449350,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776178512
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Grind.Fin.instPowFinNatOfNeZero#doc\">docs#Lean.Grind.Fin.instPowFinNatOfNeZero</a> uses <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Grind.Fin.npow#doc\">docs#Lean.Grind.Fin.npow</a>)</p>",
        "id": 585449921,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776178631
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I see now that there is a TODO in the code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- TODO: we should replace this at runtime with either repeated squaring,</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- or a GMP accelerated function.</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585450532,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776178772
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we not get the repeated squaring by default in mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 585451532,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776178966
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes we do. But there is an instance diamond here. There is the <code>grind</code> instance, and the mathlib <code>npowRecAuto</code> instance. I'm working on a PR that \"accidentally\" fixed this diamond, and instead picked the core instance.</p>",
        "id": 585451841,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776179040
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, so this is npowRec vs npowRecAuto</p>",
        "id": 585452281,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776179134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No I think it is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Grind.Fin.npow#doc\">docs#Lean.Grind.Fin.npow</a> vs <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=npowRecAuto#doc\">docs#npowRecAuto</a></p>",
        "id": 585452877,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776179193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1012x305\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/MKjDB_xC2X0wbIyIIrbFY6qH/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/MKjDB_xC2X0wbIyIIrbFY6qH/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 585453219,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776179267
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's something to be said for not just using GMP to accelerate it, but perhaps even using <code>mpz_powm_sec</code> (over <code>mpz_powm</code>). Maybe controlled by a build flag...</p>",
        "id": 585453224,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1776179269
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span>, <code>Lean.Grind.Fin.npow</code> is semireducible, so there genuinely is a diamond.</p>",
        "id": 585472141,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776183740
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Making it reducible (or just deleting it...) would I guess fix the diamond but not the performance</p>",
        "id": 585473096,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776184016
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38036\">#38036</a>, in order to not break the test for <code>ZMod</code> exponentiation, I'm overwriting Lean's <code>Fin</code> power operations.</p>",
        "id": 585473746,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1776184189
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13490\">lean#13490</a> plugs in <code>mpz_powm</code>. It's  just a draft for now, but feedback welcome.</p>",
        "id": 588509817,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1776733508
    }
]